ts in this document yourself  this is on the sherbourne school website  but i'll read through some of the  comments that really stood out to me  turing's first year at the school was in  1926  when he was aged 14 and it was said that  he had a natural bent for science but  his work was badly spoiled by extreme  untidiness now this mention of untidy or  dirty work  would become a very common thread  through a lot of these comments  his teachers used words like careless  and disappointing  and they even called his lack of  interest in french  very depressing these pages are full of  comments  saying things like his work is rather  lacking in life  or that he needs to concentrate harder  or even this note  saying that he is not a normal boy  in mathematics he ranked 10th in his  class and the comment says  not very good he spends a good deal of  time apparently in  investigations of advanced mathematics  to the neglect of his elementary work  a sound groundwork is essential in any  subject  his work is dirty i guess i agree with  the sentiment that you need to have  some good foundations before you go on  into advanced stuff  but man that comment seems really  demoralizing for a kid who is obviously  very interested in the subject turing  was indeed interested  in these investigations of advanced  mathematics  when he was aged 15 and a half he wrote  a condensed version of  einstein's general theory of relativity  as  a gift to his mother and i'll put some  pictures up of that document on the  screen for you to have a look at  i think that it's really impressive for  someone of his age to be reading  and clearly thinking about some of the  subjects and topics in that book  so i think you can clearly see he was a  talented kid  who cared for mathematics but like many  students i think  he struggled to bring this talent and  enthusiasm for science  with him through the conventional  education system  and some of these comments from his  professors  are kind of trying to 