his class for  mathematics  although the comment says that he was  easily the best mathematician in the set  so really he deserved to come first his  position  is caused again by untidiness and  carelessness his english teacher says  that  he should read more and that's  interesting because  there are also the library records of  touring available on the school's  website  and you can see that whilst he got out a  lot of books  on things like math and science he only  ever  got out three fiction books and two of  those were  part of the alice in wonderland series  by lewis carroll  and the reason he got out those books  was because one of his math teachers had  encouraged him to  since the author of alice in wonderland  lewis carroll was himself a  mathematician  and there was a lot of math sprinkled  into those stories  there are sentences like this one from  the headmaster  saying that he better take on the advice  of his teachers  if he is to achieve any real success  and that kind of hurts to read because  you know  turing's work did go on to be so  influential to mathematics and  he definitely by any standard did  achieve  real success in his field by 1930 though  things started to look a little bit more  positive  his physics teacher this time said that  he is doing much better work  the headmaster says that he seems to be  going well  and the house report says that he wins  respect  both by brains and character the  comments and pretty much every subject  including the languages  are much more positive you know we have  steady and intelligent work from the  english teacher  which is you know such a step up from  those very harsh comments at the start  they commend him for working hard and  having imagination and  interest even in his language subjects  this is the final page and the final  comments  are that he is considered pleasant and  friendly  and the headmaster has appointed him a  school prefect  they wish him success at cambridge  university  for which he had gained a scholarship  i'm happy that by the end you know all  these teachers who had been so harsh  did wish him well and and commend him  for his intelligence and his hard work  i don't know how much of that is touring  you know  becoming more mature maybe he did decide  that he did  you know need to be a lot neater to um  to really get his ideas across  and after cambridge he eventually went  on to get a phd in number theory from  princeton university  as a fun little bonus here are some  pictures of  a number theory book that turing owned  and annotated  and this book was written by john  littlewood  who you may remember from my previous  videos about the romanogen  and hardy sort of collaboration because  littlewood was also involved in that  story too  so a little bit of you know crossing  over between these two stories  another little fun fact is that alan  turing's middle name was  matheson and i kind of find that fitting  seeing as it sounds like the sun of math  although what would be more fitting  would to call tearing the  father of computer science now we can't  end on that happy note though because  tearing's life  did have a really tragic end  in 1952 he was arrested  when being gay was considered a criminal  offence  he chose to be chemically castrated  instead of going to prison  and he died two years later at the age  of 42.  he took a bite of an apple which he had  laced with cyanide  perhaps a result of the depressing  circumstances in which he found himself  in 2009 the british government issued an  apology  for the treatment of alan turing but it  remains  a really sad story and a tragic end  for one of our greatest minds and it  remains an example  of how hatred and discrimination can  rob the world of wonderful people  this part of the video is sponsored by  the great courses plus  much of alan turing's work was  philosophical in nature  he devised a test that could evaluate a  machine's ability  to exhibit intelligence he wondered  i